In article <5jl38c$n83$1@charm.magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>, milsted.1@osu.edu (Rufus Milsted) wrote:
>Does there exist, either DEC or other, a PCI Ultra-Wide SCSI host adapter 
>supported by DU 4.0? I'd like to hang a Seagate Barracuda 4LP (ST32171W) on 
>our AlphaServer 300 4/266.
>
>Thanks,
>  Rufus

Here's the answer to my question:
  DEC's part is KDPDA: PCI-to-FWSE SCSI Controller Card. (FWSE = Fast Wide 
Single Ended). Not to be confused with KDPSA: PCI-to-FWD SCSI Controller Card. 
(FWD = Fast Wide Differential.
  A third party alternative, complete with drivers for Digital UNIX is 
available from IntraServer Teechnology, Inc. See their web site at 
http://www.intraserver.com/



