As of Digital UNIX V4.0, -newc switch is the default so there is no need
to 
set that.   Also as of V4.0 with the default cc, there is no difference
between 
-O4 and -O5.   As described in the cc(1) manpage, the -O4 level contains
optimizations that may or may not help your program.  To determine
whether 
using -O4 benefits your program, you should compare program execution
times 
for the same program compiled at levels -O3 and -O4.
 
