The problem isn't so much the number of accounts as the frequency of
logins.  I'm well under 6000 accounts, but at certain times of the day
I've got a lot of people jumping on to check mail.

What makes this so annoying is that they appear to have fixed the
basic problem which was a bottleneck in the protected password data
base.  The new releases of enhanced security use an authentication
data base which would appear to present the same problem, but
experience indicates that the code is smart enough to not lock out
logins when info on a particular users last login is updated.

