:    1)   Is there any good book that will teach me shell programming
:         using the Korn shell?

http://www.amazon.com/

Do a subject search on "korn shell programming".

:    2)   How do I debug this awk problem?

:         $ x = "this+is+a+line+with+equals"
:                                
:         I am trying to replace all the + characters with spaces.

:         $ print $x | awk '{ i=gsub("+","",$0) }'
:         "@awk: There is a regular expression error.
:            *?+ not preceded by valid expression
:          The source line number is 1.
:          The error context is
:                    { i=gsub("+","",$0) >>>   <<<

"+" is a special character in regular expressions. You need to quote
it to have it treated literally:

print $x | awk '{ i=gsub("\\+"," ",$0) }'

or 

print $x | awk '{ i=gsub("[+]"," ",$0) }'

Stephen
