DEC provide some freeware software called "mtools" on the UNIX 4.0 CDROMs.
This is not installed by default in 4.0 or 4.0a but is under 4.0b.
With this software installed (and the setting of a simple symboloic link
detailed in the mtools man page) the floppy drive is accessible for
MSDOS disks using commands such as mdir, mcd and mread, etc.  By default,
the drive and the mtools will only be usable if you are logged in as root.

