Todd Graham Lewis (tlewis@mindspring.com) wrote:

: Does anyone know of any good papers on DEC's website concerning advfs?
: I'm interested in how to set up dynamically-extensible volumes (throw in a
: 2GB disk, add it to the logical device, have 2GB additional on that
: device, take disks out & shrink it, etc.)

The utilities you'll find yourself using to do that are:

mkfdmn		- make a file domain from a physical disk partition
mkfset		- make a fileset (mountable entity) within a file domain
addvol		- add a physical disk partition to an existing file domain

balance		- evenly distribute disk usage among physical disk partitions
		  of a file domain
defragment	- defragment files in a file domain

rmvol		- remove a physical disk partition from a file domain
rmfdmn		- remove a file domain completely

: Names of man pages are equally welcome.  TIA.

"man advfs" has lots of stuff, including the complete summary of advfs
related entities and commands that operate on those entities.

Stephen
