Robin Rowe <rower@ise1.saic.com> wrote:
> Hi. We have an Alphastation 600 that we are adding a second ethernet
> card to. How do I get the machine to recognize the second ethernet card?

> The SCSI and 10-baseT card are integrated to the same board so we have
> to keep that and add the 100-baseTX (DEC DE500AA). There are absolutely
> no instructions for how to do this that came with the card, nor have I
> found anything very useful in dxbook, etc. We did a firmware upgrade
> which fixed a boot problem we had with the new card, but DEC support
> doesn't seem to be able to help us beyond that.

> OSF1 V3.2 41 alpha

Robin,

	1) Install the card into an open PCI Slot.

	2) You are going to have to get the proper device entries
	   into the system configuration file for the new card. The
	   file I am talking about is  /sys/conf/SYSTEMNAME

	   There are several ways to do it. I prefer to boot with
	   /genvmunix and run /usr/sbin/sizer -n new. That gives
	   you a device file called /tmp/new which you can compare
	   with your current config file to get the new device entry.

	3) Once you have the proper device entries in the config file
	   rebuild the kernel.

	4) You need to run /usr/sbin/netsetup to configure the new card.

							Steve
 








