> I have a user who keeps getting the following message sent to them. The
> machine is running DUNIX 4.0. The user reads their mail with mailx. Is
> it SENDMAIL or mailx creating this message and for what reason. 

Neither created this.  It was placed there by an IMAP server, meaning
that your user is likely to have tried to access his or her mail using
an IMAP client (such as PINE).  If the user now uses mailx regularly,
then it is safe to delete the message; the only loss will be of some
indexing information used by the IMAP server and nothing else.  If he or
she should use an IMAP client again, it will come back.

