The more general and up-to-date answer at this time (4.x systems)
is to add options of the form:

	[-screen<n> <width>[x<height>]] [-vsync<n> <rate>]

Where:

<n>		Logical screen number beginning at 0.
<width>		Desired screen width from those supported.
<height>	Desired screen height from those supported.
<rate>		Vertical retrace rate, in Hz, from those supported.

E.g.:

	-screen0 1920x1200 -vsync0 65 -screen1 1024x864 -vsync1 60

Release notes may describe the supported resolutions and rates
for various cards, further limited by your monitor's capabilities,
and some current products extend to 1920x1200 as suggested by
the example.

If you use CDE, after editing the Xserver.conf file, you need only
select the 'Reset login screen' option from the login window to
use the new options.

