: One note on gated or routed:

: When you run netsetup, it just asks if you want to run "gated" or
: "routed".  I've also found that you have to set "ROUTER=YES" in
: /etc/rc.config (then reboot) for DUX to forward packets.

It should ask if you're going to be a router as well.

: I don't know why, I just do that and routing starts working.

Setting ROUTER="yes" in /etc/rc.config causes the command "iprsetup -s"
to be executed at startup (see /sbin/init.d/inet), which sets the
values of the kernel variables ipforwarding and ipgateway accordingly.

Check the man page for iprsetup for details. You don't need to reboot
if you run iprsetup by hand (although you might want to restart or
reconfig gated).

