I am not sure if this is the right newsgroup, but I hope someone
in Digital headquarters will read it and help.

The story:
 - We bought a DWPVC-BA (i.e. a Bit3 model 617 PCI to VME
   adapter including software for Digital Unix) beginning of 97
   from EBV.
 - While the Digital unix software was running basically fine
   from the start (a bug fix was provided by Lee Parker/DEC
   recently) we found trouble in the arbitration of the vme card
   on the slave side (arbitration between slave vme access and
   shared memory access).
 - The same problems we saw with Bit3 VME cards purchased from
   Meilhaus (EBV was not able to sell those).
 - I asked Jim Terpstra of Bit3 for help, he found out (from
   the serial numbers) that our VME cards are at revision G,
   should be at "K", and the pci cards are at "L", should be
   at "Q". And he said the problem we see was explicitly fixed
   by those higher revisions.
   And he advised to get revision upgrades (free of charge by
   Bit3) through the dealers.
 - I also looked at DECs Software product description (on the web).
   It requires revision J for the VME side, revision P for the
   pci side. Remember: I got shipped revisions G (VME) and L (PCI).
 - On March 22 I contacted both Meilhaus and EBV.
   Meilhaus meanwhile upgraded their equipment (they sent me
   replacement modules while mine are being upgraded).
 - EBV (for the DWPVC-BA) handed the case over to Digital
   service center in Munich, call # 33348, on March 25.
 - Since then I was contacted by several people. Everyone
   I told (and faxed) the story from the beginning. Everyone said
   he/she would take care of it. After a few days someone else was
   in charge, and so on.
 - I am a bit tired (after almost 4 weeks) to wait for 
   Digital Munich to respond to this call and propose a time
   schedule for the upgrade. Actually I have given up in 
   expecting them to do anything at all in the matter, except
   of handing over the case from person to person.
