Hello Scott,
did you use the -x and -p options when you created your file domain?
Here's the relevant bit from "man mkfdmn":

"Systems with file domains that contain very large numbers of files can use
more metadata extents (similar to inodes in UFS) than normal.  By default,
AdvFS attempts to grow the metadata table by 128 pages each time
additional metadata extents are needed. Frequent requests by the system to 
increase the metadata table causes the metadata to become very fragmented 
which can result in an "out of disk space" error.

You can reduce the amount of metadata fragmentation in one of two ways: by
increasing the number of pages the system attempts to grow the metadata
table each time more space is needed or by preallocating all of the
space for the metadata table when the file domain is created."
      

Hope it helps...

