>no instructions for how to do this that came with the card, nor have I
>found anything very useful in dxbook, etc. We did a firmware upgrade
>which fixed a boot problem we had with the new card, but DEC support
>doesn't seem to be able to help us beyond that.
>
Hi Robin,

its very easy to implement a new controller:

1. boot genvmunix and watch the given controller detect messages
    (you can use uerf -R -r 300 |more after booting)
2. use doconfig to generate a new kernel option file and rebuild the kernel
3. set the ewa0_mode and ewb0_mode variable on console mode to the requested
    port mode (BNC, twisted, aui) to prevent the message "carrier not found"

let me guess, you have no agreement with dec? Because all support engineers (except some
poor guys here) at the support office have this information.................

Regards






