: my UNIX system.

...<snip>...

: 2. I am using CuteFTP to tranfer files from DOS to UNIX and when i do
: this alle the files in is uppercase, and i need them in lowercase. Is
: there a utility in OSF/1 to convert the filenames or where can i get a
: program / script that can do this.

Put the following one line script in your path in a file (say), 'lcase':

mv $1 `echo $1 | awk '{print tolower($0)}'`

Then use : 

	lcase <filename>

to convert the filename to lowercase.

One question to you wizards out there. Actually, this command is small
enough  to warrent being an alias. But the single quote (') character
required in the awk command makes it very difficult. Any idea how you
could make lcase into an alias instead of an one line executable file?
