> simply the configuration of our Alpha and oSF1 on it.
> --
> POPULUS, the Intelligent People Locator -- http://www.POPULUS.net/

The maximum number of processes is controlled by the maxusers macro
(or variable or whatever) in /sys/conf/HOSTNAME. Change that from the
default 32 to something larger - maybe 128 or 256 - and rebuild the
kernel. A possibly forking web server with many accesses running lots
of CGI scripts etc will consume a lot of processes. There are also
some tips on kernel tuning Digital Unix for Web services on
www.digital.com.

/Erik

