frey@otter.bme.unc.edu (Eric Frey) wrote:
>I have an AlphaServer 1000 running Digital Unix and a DE435 Etherworks
>Turbo PCI Ethernet Controller. I want to get it to run in Full Duplex
>mode. The manual seems to say it will autoconfigure, but this doesn't
>seem to work. I am trying to attach it to a Cabletron switch (mmac8 I think),
>which does not support autonegotiation. However, I had the network guys
>set the switch for full duplex, shutdown, cylcled the power, rebooted, and
>it didn't work. The manual discusses utilities for DOS that presumably could
>be used to force the card into full duplex mode. Does anyone have any
>ideas how I can do that under Digital Unix? Thanks for any help.
>
it is only autonegotiated under decunix < 3.2c. Versions >= 3.2c must explicit set the
environment variable ewa0_mode/ewb0_mode to fastfd (only for fast ethernet supported!)
Be sure you have executed the "init" command and powercycled the machine after
changing the variable. Be sure your bridge/router is properly configured!

Regards

  Ralf





