We have come across a problem with the Quantum Fireball 3.2GB disk drive and
the wide SCSI controller on Digital 500 and 600 Alphastations, running
DU3.2 and DU4.0B. We are trying to add an extra drive to an existing system.
The additional Quantum drive can be seen by "show dev" at the console
prompt, but the system dies on boot at the stage where it is determining
which drives are attached to which controller (in the case of the 600, which
has two wide controllers) or which drives are attached to the only controller
in the case of the 500. It does not appear to be a cable or termination
problem (we've changed cables, the high byte termination has been set
at the console prompt for the relevant controller (since the Fireball is
a narrow device), and other narrow drives work happily on these machines). The
only other thing is that the / and /usr partitions on these machines are
running the AdvFS. If they are configured as ufs partitions instead, the system
boots OK with the Quantum drive in the chain.
BTW, the Quantums are quite happy if connected to a narrow SCSI controller.
The critical combination of circumstances seems to be:
Quantum Fireball 3.2GB + Wide SCSI controller + AdvFS on system disk = NO GO.
Has anyone else experienced anything like this? DEC...?
Thanks in advance...
