David Yanuk <dave@atmos.umd.edu> writes:
> Has anyone experienced the following:
> 
> JavaScripts will not execute with NEtscape-3.0
> running DEC UNIX 4.0. The java class files (java_30)
> are copied to all recommended locations. Java is enabled
> within Netscape via Options|Network|Languages.
> 
> No errors are logged when the Java console is opened.
> Gray box appears were the Java Applet should be executing.

There's only a Netscape-3.0 for Dig. UNIX 3.2 (not for 4.0) and 
unfortunately some X11 library calls seem to be incompatible from 
3.2 to 4.0. The only workaround DEC could offer is to force Netscape 
to use the old libs:

- copy libX{11,ext,m,mu,t}.so from a system with DEC UNIX 3.2{c,d}
  to a directory /path/to/netscape/libs
- create a wrapper for netscape that sets LD_LIBRARY_PATH to
  /path/to/netscape/libs:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH and then calls the netscape
  binary itself

Ugly hack, but works. Same is true for Netscape 3.01 (haven't tried
the 4.0b{2,3} on DU 4.0 since it has major bugs).

HTH,
Thomas Anders.

