Look for a utility by the name of xmodmap.  This will remap the keys in the
X-Server.  

Your question is being posted in an Digital UNIX related news group, but
you mention OpenVMS, so I am a little confused.  I know that xmodmap is
available on OpenVMS (only I don't remember where they hide it or if they
stick a prefix infront of the name (like maybe DECW$XMODMAP or something
like that - it has been too long since I looked at OpenVMS - my memory is
not that good).

On Digital UNIX, there is xmodmap and a man page to describe its use.

But even better on Digital UNIX is the utility dxkeycaps.  The best way to
access this is via the Digital UNIX Session Manager Keyboard Options and
click on the "Edit Keycaps..." button on the right center of the dialog
box.  There is also a man page on dxkeycaps.  I do not think dxkeycaps is
available for OpenVMS, but I could be wrong - like I said it has been a
long time.

