Doug Hamilton wrote:
> 
> What DEC modules do I need installed in order to use C compiler?
> 
> I keep getting library errors, e.g. can't find stdio.h.
That does not make sense. The C compiler is shipped on the base product. 
Make sure that you installed the Development Environment subset. stdio.h
should be in /usr/include. What compilation options are you using. One
thing that could cause this is misuse of the -I command line option. On
Digital Unix, -I alone tels the compiler not to look in the standard
place for header files. Also, there is a search hierarchy for libraries.
The -L flag, similar to the -I flag, used without an argument tells the
linker not to look in the standard place. Both the CFE (the default
compiler in V3.2 and prior), and DECC (V4.0 and later) support these
flags. 
