> How do I extract file1, file2, etc., from $@ or any of internal macros
> to form new marco AAA to be used in later part of my Makefile? I tried 

You don't. make macros are static can't be redefined by commands within
the makefile. If you seriously needed to do this, you can do cascaded
makefiles:

        $(FLIST):
                AAA=`...` $(MAKE) $(MAKEFLAGS) target

Thus make calls make, and in the second call, the value of the environment
variable AAA is available as a make macro.

