In article <mele-0304970648200001@dial58.bulloch.com>, Melvin C. Etheridge <mele@telconet.com> wrote:
> Help!!!!   

> I have a LSM/ADVFS volume under DU4.0 consisting of two 9 gig drives and
> cannot get above 69-70% and expires just start taking days to complete!!!
>  
> Any ideas anyone???

Many.

Advfs and News (or, more particularly, any application creating and
deleting lots and lots of small files) do not get along. If you didn't
use the Advfs options to pre-allocated metadata, this is what
happens. If this isn't a production system, the simplest thing
to do is just blow it away and start over, probably using UFS
rather than Advfs. If it is a production system, defragment a lot
(do you have the Advfs utilities license?), and tune your expire
to not get above 60%. 

This isn't a Digital Unix issue, per se, but news would be far,
far better off on 9 2-gig disks, rather than 2 9-gig disks. 
Do you have everything, including history, logs, overview and the
spool on that volume? 

As for the expires taking days to complete, this seems to be a
new 4.0 syndrome. There's at least one other message in news.software.nntp
about this same thing, with the assertion that it's a Digital Unix
bug.

	- Saul

