Dan's analysis is exactly correct. The V3.2x version of CDE was an 
unsupported Advanced Developers Kit. In it, neither dtlogin or dtsession
(for password checking during screen locks) was updated to use SIA. That's
the primary reason you couldn't use the ADK on a system running C2 security.
As of V4.0, SIA is in use in dtlogin/dtgreet, and dtsession.

Chris



