[...]

> Inodes, et. all look good with only about 7% used at 70% capacity:
> Filesystem                512-blocks        Used            Available
> Capacity     Iused            Ifree         %Iused  Mounted on

> lsmdom#lsmfset       35532800    17127900    15422576    53%    
> 1465070    29743945     5%   /news

Advfs doesn't have inodes. What that command is reporting, I have no
idea, but it's almost certainly irrelevant.

> I would like to use UFS, but it will not support spanning two drives will it?

If you use LSM to encapsulate the disks, it looks like one big disk.

Life is full of tradeoffs:

	- you can use Advfs, and live with the maintenance issues
	- you can use UFS, and live with the fsck time

In either case, you're going to have to rebuild your news spool, to
make it work. For advfs, you'll need to increase the metadata extents
and sizes; for ufs, you'll have to create the ufs file system.

