Warren Castle (castle@adminnet.assiniboinec.mb.ca) wrote:
: I have a Kron shell menu script that I don't what the end users to get out of.
: Which signals should I trap?  I tried trapping all of them and while this did 
: prevent them from breaking out of the script, it also left orphan processes on 
: the system.  If a user closed thier telnet app without logging out first, thier 
: process remained on the system.
: 
: Thanks.
: Warren Castle, Network Manager 

	The signals that you can generate from the keyboard are the
ones you usually need to worry about - SIGINT (signal 2 generated by
ctrl-C) SIGQUIT (signal 3 generated by ctrl-\). In some cases you
might want to trap adds SIGHUP (signal 1) and sometimes SIGTERM (signal 15).
In short, at least

	trap ""  2 3

but probably not more than 

	trap ""  1 2 3 15

