Floyd Davenport (davenportf@idea.ag.uiuc.edu) wrote:
: Ever since we upgraded to DEC Unix 4.0, any alias we create with
: a capital letter is not recognized.  Sendmail doesn't complain, it
: just doesn't see the alias.  When we change the capital to lower
: case, it works just fine.
: 
: Has anyone experienced this problem or is there some new default in
: the Sendmail configuration that I need to reset?
: 
: Floyd Davenport
: College of ACES
: University of Illinios
: davenportf@idea.ag.uiuc.edu

	The folks at DEC have done it again! :) Here is the

Mlocal line from 3.2D-2:

Mlocal, P=/bin/mail, F=rlsDFMmn, S=10, R=20, A=mail -r $f -d $u

and from 4.0A:

Mlocal, P=/bin/mail, F=lsDFMmnu, S=10, R=20, A=mail -r $f -d $u

Notice that they slipped a 'u' in there. Taking that out should
solve your problem. If the alias you are talking about came from
a sendmail-built alias file, the alias gets converted to a lower
case anway (if from NIS, makedbm probably built it and probably
does not get converted). But the 'u' mailer flag says to preserve
the case of the user. Brian gets converted to brian in the alias
files, but mail to Brian doesn't go anywhere because there is
no Brian alias exists (just brian) and sendmail is not converting
the address to lower case because the 'u' flag is set.

