Yao-Lu Tsai wrote:

> I am trying to port my C codes from SUNOS/Solaris to DEC UNIX 3.2.
> I found DEC UNIX is a 64-bit OS. The long and pointer data type
> are 64-bit. Unfortunately, there are MANY MANY type casting between
> "int" and pointer in my C codes. 
I won't comment on the coding practice. However, the Digital Unix
calling standard states that the first 6 parameters passed to a function
are passed by register. Likewise, functions return parameters as
registers. (Passing structs and returning structs is a bit different). 
There is a 32 bit library that contains libc functions that are 32-64
bit sensitive. 
Also, there are some tools that Digital provides that can assist you in
porting. There is the Porting Assistant, which is part of FUSE, and
lint. The lint -Q option was specifically implemented to find 32-64bit
problems. 

